From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wslg-patches <patches@localhost>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rdprail-shell: give xdg_popup RAIL windows their parent as
 owner

#169 makes the input panel a RAIL window owned by the toplevel holding the
text_input (JBR binds text-input on the toplevel). Windows raises the whole
owner tree when it activates an owned window, so an xdg_popup without an
owner (rdprail.c only sets one for wl_subsurface) drops behind its own
toplevel the instant the fcitx5 candidate window appears: the Ctrl+N popup
"disappears" and comes back when the candidate window closes and weston
resends the Z order. weston's own Z order and views are correct throughout;
the problem is purely on the Windows side.

Fix: when a popup is mapped (popup_state_changed hook from #172), set its
RAIL owner to its parent xdg surface via #169's set_window_owner.
weston_desktop_surface_get_parent() was only declared in internal.h and is
now exported for shell plugins.
---
 include/libweston-desktop/libweston-desktop.h |  2 ++
 libweston-desktop/surface.c                   |  2 +-
 rdprail-shell/shell.c                         | 23 +++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/libweston-desktop/libweston-desktop.h b/include/libweston-desktop/libweston-desktop.h
index aeb5bc5a..eb9affe1 100644
--- a/include/libweston-desktop/libweston-desktop.h
+++ b/include/libweston-desktop/libweston-desktop.h
@@ -200,6 +200,8 @@ struct weston_desktop_client *
 weston_desktop_surface_get_client(struct weston_desktop_surface *surface);
 struct weston_surface *
 weston_desktop_surface_get_surface(struct weston_desktop_surface *surface);
+struct weston_desktop_surface *
+weston_desktop_surface_get_parent(struct weston_desktop_surface *surface);
 const char *
 weston_desktop_surface_get_title(struct weston_desktop_surface *surface);
 const char *
diff --git a/libweston-desktop/surface.c b/libweston-desktop/surface.c
index 1894609e..579e1e23 100644
--- a/libweston-desktop/surface.c
+++ b/libweston-desktop/surface.c
@@ -701,7 +701,7 @@ weston_desktop_surface_get_implementation_data(struct weston_desktop_surface *su
 	return surface->implementation_data;
 }
 
-struct weston_desktop_surface *
+WL_EXPORT struct weston_desktop_surface *
 weston_desktop_surface_get_parent(struct weston_desktop_surface *surface)
 {
 	return surface->parent;
diff --git a/rdprail-shell/shell.c b/rdprail-shell/shell.c
index 1f293334..9c338320 100644
--- a/rdprail-shell/shell.c
+++ b/rdprail-shell/shell.c
@@ -3412,10 +3412,29 @@ desktop_popup_state_changed(struct weston_desktop_surface *desktop_surface,
 			    bool mapped, void *data)
 {
 	struct desktop_shell *shell = data;
+	struct weston_surface *surface =
+		weston_desktop_surface_get_surface(desktop_surface);
+
+	/* Keep popups in their parent's RAIL owner tree: Windows raises the
+	 * whole owner tree when it activates an owned window (e.g. the input
+	 * panel owned by the toplevel), so an unowned popup would be covered
+	 * by its own toplevel. */
+	if (mapped && shell->rdprail_api->set_window_owner) {
+		struct weston_desktop_surface *parent =
+			weston_desktop_surface_get_parent(desktop_surface);
+
+		if (parent) {
+			struct weston_surface *owner =
+				weston_surface_get_main_surface(
+					weston_desktop_surface_get_surface(parent));
+
+			if (owner && owner != surface)
+				shell->rdprail_api->set_window_owner(surface, owner);
+		}
+	}
 
 	if (shell->rdprail_api->notify_popup_state)
-		shell->rdprail_api->notify_popup_state(
-			weston_desktop_surface_get_surface(desktop_surface), mapped);
+		shell->rdprail_api->notify_popup_state(surface, mapped);
 }
 
 static const struct weston_desktop_api shell_desktop_api = {
